[h1]Sublime Porte: Ottoman Reforged[/h1]

Take command of the Ottoman Empire in 1836. Decide what survives, what must change, and what the Sublime Porte becomes.

Guide the Tanzimat, face constitutional politics and foreign pressure, and modernize the state. Then choose between Ottomanism, Islamism, and Turkism.

History gives you opportunities. Great-power status must be earned.

[h2]Campaign Tree[/h2]
The Campaign Tree is the spine of the run. Open it from the sidebar:

Tanzimat → Constitutional Question (Meşrutiyet Meselesi) → Three Policies (Üç Tarz-ı Siyaset) → Ottomanism, Islamism, or Turkism.

Each node shows live requirements, so you can see what still blocks the next step. After Tanzimat, the constitutional question has to close — Young Ottomans, the Kanun-i Esasi, or a palace path — before the three policies unlock.

[SCREENSHOT: Campaign Tree]

[h2]Three political paths[/h2]
[SCREENSHOT: Three Policies]

[b]OTTOMANISM[/b]
Reform and constitutionalize the Empire. Equality, press, and franchise. There is no conquest tree.

[b]ISLAMISM[/b]
Strengthen the Caliphate and project influence across the Muslim world — Arabia, the Nile, and the Maghreb. The Caliph can call for support. The path ends as a Great Caliphate on the Ottoman tag.

[b]TURKISM[/b]
Pursue the Turanian Ideal through staged claims. Remain the Ottoman Empire, or proclaim the Great Ottoman Empire. The country is never renamed Turan.

[h2]Historical events and diplomacy[/h2]
[SCREENSHOT: Historical Event]

Egypt can close as a limited Levant settlement, a costly maximalist victory, or a stalemate. Hünkâr İskelesi and Baltalimanı are opening choices, not flavour text. Russia presses the Eastern Question. Rumelia, Bedirhan, an Armenian Question after Berlin, Tripoli, Tunis, Aden, and muhacir waves all put weight on the treasury and the provinces.

History provides the pressure; the player decides the outcome.

[h2]Learning from Europe[/h2]
[SCREENSHOT: Modernization]

Send students, officers, technicians, and educators to France, Britain, Prussia/Germany, or Austria. Capacity is limited. You choose a partner, live with the trade-offs, and modernize what you can actually sustain.

[h2]Court, companies, and flavor[/h2]
Start in Topkapı, build Dolmabahçe, and move the court. Found Şirket-i Hayriye on the Bosphorus, or face the Imperial Ottoman Bank as a later concession. Quiet years still feel like the Porte — and custom Ottoman-inspired music tracks play while you do.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Victoria 3[/b] 1.13.* (tested on 1.13.11)
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3385002128]Community Mod Framework[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3654153829]Community State Framework[/url]
[/list]
[b]Load order:[/b] Community Mod Framework → Community State Framework → Sublime Porte: Ottoman Reforged

National Awakening is optional. With it off, the campaign still runs; Great Eastern Crisis journal content simply does not appear. Voice of the People and Sphere of Influence are also optional.

Start a [b]new campaign[/b]. This mod does not use [code]replace_path[/code]. Other large Ottoman overhauls that edit the same areas may conflict.

English is the source language. Turkish is fully supported.

[h2]A note from the author[/h2]
This is my first mod. I have tried to research the subjects carefully and keep the implementation close to working vanilla patterns, but a project of this size will inevitably have areas that need correction or further balancing.

Historical corrections are welcome, especially when accompanied by a source.

For bug reports, please open a GitHub Issue (English or Turkish form): [url=https://github.com/oguzhanaslan/mod-sublime-porte-ottoman-reforged/issues/new/choose]GitHub Issues[/url]

Please include:
[list]
[*]Your Victoria 3 version
[*]Enabled DLC
[*]Your full mod list and load order
[*]Whether you started a new campaign
[*]The relevant save file or [code]error.log[/code], if available
[/list]

Thank you for reading, and I hope the mod gives the Ottoman campaign the sense of continuity, difficulty and possibility that I felt it was missing.

